# AWARE .npmignore
# Created 2026-08-02 per Alvin directive (msg 2116): exclude React UI deps from npm tarball.
#
# Updated 2026-11-10 (scribe): defence in depth for the npm public-boundary
# leak. `npm publish` had been run from the repository working tree rather
# than from a clean checkout of the release tag, so npm packed 27 files that
# were neither committed nor tagged — including the investor pitch deck, the
# pitch PDF/HTML, and a stray src/coordinator/http-server.js.bak. The
# package.json "files" whitelist is now an explicit enumeration of docs/
# subdirectories; the rules below are the second lock on the same door.
#
# NOTE: .npmignore only applies to files that are NOT in the package.json
# "files" whitelist. The whitelist is the primary control. This file is the
# belt to that suspenders. The durable control is scripts/publish-guard.mjs,
# which refuses to publish a tarball that does not match the tag.

# React UI dependencies (huge — 88 MB / 77k files if not excluded)
src/ui/node_modules/
src/ui/build/
src/ui/.cache/

# Generated seed data (defense in depth — also fixed in .gitignore)
/src/data/users.json
/src/data/agents.json

# Internal / non-publishable document trees.
# docs/ is enumerated in package.json "files"; these are belt-and-suspenders
# so a future edit that re-adds a broad "docs/" entry cannot re-open the leak.
docs/investor/
docs/research/
docs/design/
docs/private/

# Editor / backup / scratch artefacts that must never ship.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
